# For more information on these fields, see:
# https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/adding_to_third_party.md#readme_chromium
#
# TaffyGo vendors this engine under //taffy rather than under Chromium's
# //third_party/rust because the matching engine is a TaffyGo product
# decision (0086), not an upstream one, and because Chromium's regex crate
# is test-only while this plane needs it on the request path.

Name: adblock-rust
Short Name: adblock
URL: https://github.com/brave/adblock-rust/
Version: 0.13.3
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: MPL-2.0
License File: vendor/adblock-v0_13/LICENSE
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: yes

Description:
The matching engine behind Ads and trackers: network-request blocking and
cosmetic filtering for the EasyList family. Reached from filtering.core
through a C ABI in c_abi/; TaffyGo's own Cargo workspace crates are not
linked into the browser process. Transitive crates.io dependencies sit
beside it under vendor/.

User-facing copy does not name this crate, Brave, or Shields.

Local Modifications:
Cargo.toml drops the js/ and fuzz/ workspace members, disables the
single-thread feature so Engine is Send+Sync, and leaves css-validation
off. The C ABI and GN cargo_crate graph are first-party glue.
`$genericblock` is parsed (no `gblock` alias), stored on its own network
list, and causes matching to skip the generic bucket when the option is
active; `$important` generic rules still match. `$generichide` is
unchanged.
